{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>The children of Ephraim</b> — By way of derash, all Israel are called thus, as in: 'Is Ephraim a dear son to me.' Also an allusion to the children of Ephraim who departed Egypt before the appointed time had arrived, and the allusion is in Chronicles: 'and the men of Gath slew them, and Ephraim their father mourned.' And according to the peshat, the main thrust of this psalm concerns the kingdom of David and the building of Mount Zion, where the ark was during David's reign, after Shiloh — which belonged to the children of Ephraim — was destroyed. Therefore: 'and the tribe of Ephraim He did not choose' — at the end, after He had chosen them first, to cause His name to dwell in Shiloh. And the faithful witness for this interpretation: 'the tribe of Ephraim, bearers of bows' — they are the men of Shiloh, concerning whom it is said afterward: 'they did not keep the covenant of Elohim.' And further: 'He performed wonders before their fathers' — and this was after Israel came forth from Egypt." "<b>Those who bear</b> — Defective of kof, like אש אוכלה. And the word נושקי is attached to קשת, in the manner of נהרי נחלי דבש וחמאה. And the meaning is that they turned their backs on the day of battle — a metaphor, because they did not keep the covenant of Elohim, who caused His glory to dwell among them." "And some say: as is the practice of bearers of bows, that they do not stand in one place, so did the children of Ephraim turn."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 78, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra quotes Jeremiah 31:19 (הבן יקיר לי אפרים) and 1 Chronicles 7:21; the verse 'שבט אפרים רומי קשת' is from Psalm 78:9 itself, and 'ובשבט אפרים לא בחר' from Psalm 78:67.", 1 "Ibn Ezra reads נושקי as defective (missing final kof), i.e., נושק rather than נושקים; the analogy is to construct-chain attachment where the first noun modifies the second."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:35:02.741315124Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}